@startuml grant-issue-and-check
!theme plain
' Updated: accepted architecture-review findings (2026-10-13)
title Grants (v1.3): issuing by the owner, delegating with attenuation only, checking at every point of action, revoking

actor "Owner\n(client app, root key)" as OW
participant "Trust gateway\n(signed changes in)" as TG
participant "Trust registry\n(grants, bindings, revocations)" as T
participant "Orchestrator\n(OS user orch_a)" as O
participant "Key keeper" as KK
participant "Launch dispatcher" as D
participant "Session host" as SH
participant "Bridge\n(broker)" as BR
participant "Task core\n(board, kguard)" as B

== issue ==
OW -> OW: separate grants, actions[] entries from the register:\nsession.input for session X; session.approve bound to target.execution_id;\nsession.control for the concrete control target; expires_at, delegable: no
note over OW, SH
  The subject uses an operator key enrolled for the binding (ADM §§3–4).
  transcript is the binding audience projection (ADM §7),
  separate from session action authority; no generic operator action.
end note
OW -> TG: signed grant record
TG -> T: verify owner signature; append; new revocation snapshot id
T --> BR: snapshot refresh (broker, host, dispatcher, core subscribe)

== delegate (attenuation only) ==
O -> KK: sign grant {issuer: orch_a, subject: w_17, action: post to thread t,\ntarget: room r, expiry ≤ own} (peer UID → key of orch_a)
KK --> O: signature
O -> TG: delegated grant
TG -> T: check: orch_a holds a delegable grant covering\n(action, target) ⊇ the new grant? expiry not longer?
alt wider than the issuer's own
  T --> O: refused{amplification}
else subset
  T -> T: append; chain recorded (owner → orch_a → w_17)
end

== check at the point of action ==
D -> T: spawn role R in P by orch_a? requested child grants ⊆ delegable?
SH -> T: enqueue user_turn to X by sender S? (session.input, fresh, not revoked)
BR -> T: may S write to a_7? (post/mailbox grant)
B -> T: may run R move element E from s1 to s2? (role grant under the flow version)
note over D, B
  One verification library everywhere: parse, verify the signature
  chain to the root, check expiry and conditions, consult the
  revocation snapshot. The requester never judges its own request.
end note

== revoke ==
OW -> TG: signed revocation of the grant (or of an identity)
TG -> T: append; snapshot id bumps
T --> SH: refresh; in-flight items re-admitted at dispatch against the new snapshot
@enduml
